        "id": 361
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T13:57:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "An inline-only WQE leaves the buffer tail unchanged. If subsequent non-inline packets fill the buffer ring before its successful CQE is processed, `buf_tail \u003d\u003d txq-\u003ehead` and the second check sees exactly `buf_sz` outstanding buffers. This valid state sets `txq-\u003eerror` and permanently stops TX. Could we allow this case and validate the completed WQE against the outstanding SQ entries?",
      "revId": "5824118f828e40cc822ffd3e04216b42f6c521c1",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8c35c1e9_64863d98",
        "filename": "src/plugins/rdma/output.c",
        "patchSetId": 26
      },
      "lineNbr": 471,
      "author": {
        "id": 361
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T13:57:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When the fast path has already posted packets and the remaining packets are all too short, this loop drops them without updating `last`. It still points at the next unused SQ slot, so the final doorbell targets an unposted WQE and the posted packets lack a completion request. Could we preserve the last posted WQE across the fallback and drops? A frame containing four valid packets followed by four short packets reproduces this.",
      "revId": "5824118f828e40cc822ffd3e04216b42f6c521c1",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17ac5d0c_f0b5ddda",
